E2A9                             ; ---- machine code: the grave
E2A9                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
E2A9                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (60h) is
E2A9                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
E2A9                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ); see the
E2A9                             ; contract in the header.
E2A9   20 1C E4     H_GRAVE:   JSR   rdhex   
E2AC   B0 1C                  BCS   exec   
E2AE   0A           HX1:      ASL      
E2AF   0A                     ASL      
E2B0   0A                     ASL      
E2B1   0A                     ASL      
E2B2   85 04                  STA   T0   
E2B4   20 1C E4               JSR   rdhex   
E2B7   B0 0C                  BCS   hx2   ; odd digit: already consumed, dropped
E2B9   05 04                  ORA   T0   
E2BB   81 00                  STA   (0,X)   ; (never checked)
E2BD   20 80 E2               JSR   inctos   
E2C0   20 1C E4               JSR   rdhex   
E2C3   90 E9                  BCC   hx1   
E2C5   A9 60        HX2:      LDA   #60h   
E2C7   81 00                  STA   (0,X)   
E2C9   60                     RTS      
